<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wheat harvest 37.6 pct over - gov't.</title>
<headline>Argentine wheat harvest 37.6 pct over - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 37.6 percent of their 1996/97 wheat crop by December 13, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>The Secretariat calculated that eventual output would be 15.2 million tonnes, if weather conditions held. It said it assumed an average yield of 2.29 tonnes per hectare harvested. Maize sowing was 83.0 percent complete, soybean sowing 66.9 percent over and sunflower sowing 92.1 percent complete. Cotton sowing was 71.0 percent concluded, and sorghum sowing 68.6 percent finished.</p>
</text>
